URL: https://github.com/wixtoolset/wix3/releases/download/wix3112rtm/wix311-binaries.zip
Version: 3.11.2.4516
License: MS-RL
License File: LICENSE

Description:
The Windows Installer XML (WiX) is a toolset that builds Windows installation
packages from XML source code. The toolset supports a command line environment
that developers may integrate into their build processes to build MSI and MSM
setup packages.

This is WiX 3.11.2, the last release of the 3.x line that does not require
.NET Framework 4.

Why not 3.14, which is the newest 3.x:
  3.14's binaries are compiled against the v4.0.30319 runtime and its
  candle.exe.config carries no fallback, so .NET Framework 4 becomes a build
  prerequisite. 3.11.2 is compiled against v2.0.50727 and lists both v4.0 and
  v2.0.50727 as supported runtimes, with useLegacyV2RuntimeActivationPolicy
  set -- so it runs on .NET 2.0/3.5 and on 4.x alike, which is strictly more
  compatible than either neighbour. There is no 3.12 or 3.13, so this is the
  immediate predecessor rather than a compromise several versions back.

Local Modifications:
Only the top level of the upstream zip is vendored. doc/ and sdk/ are not,
which is what takes this from 100MB to 14MB -- less than half the 31MB the
WiX 3.0.5419 copy occupied.

  doc/  4.2MB of toolset documentation, not read by any build step.
  sdk/  82MB, almost all of it sdk/vs2010 through sdk/vs2017: the Visual
        Studio integration packages. Nothing here drives WiX from Visual
        Studio; sawbuck/installer/installer.gyp shells out to candle.exe and
        light.exe directly.

The root level is kept whole rather than reduced to the files actually
loaded. That is a rule a future upgrade can follow without re-deriving it,
and it cannot silently omit a dependency the way a hand-picked list can.
Everything the build touches is there: candle.exe and light.exe with their
.config files, WixUIExtension.dll and WixUtilExtension.dll for the -ext
arguments, darice.cub for the ICE validation the -sice: flags filter, wix.dll
which both drivers load, and Microsoft.Deployment.WindowsInstaller.dll.

Also not vendored: x86/burn.exe, the Burn bootstrapper, which only matters
for building bundles. Sawbuck ships a plain MSI.

Note on the licence:
WiX 3.0.5419 was CPL and shipped a CPL.TXT; the project relicensed to the
Microsoft Reciprocal License before 3.11, and copyright now sits with the
.NET Foundation. The LICENSE file beside this one is upstream's LICENSE.TXT.
